# Standard library

`std` is built into `nml`: its modules are imported as `std.name`, with no configuration. `nml init` and the language server write their sources to `.nml/std/`, for editors to show.

## std.toc {#toc}

`:toc` lists the document's headings, nested by level and numbered like them, with an optional title.

```
:import std.toc

:toc Contents
```

Here is this page's:

:toc On this page

Headings with the class `unlisted` are left out, and those with `unnumbered` are listed without a number. The list is made once the whole document is parsed, so it can come before the headings.

## std.nav {#nav}

`:nav` lists the workspace's pages, grouped by category. It is made when the page is linked, so it follows pages as they are added, removed or renamed. This documentation's sidebar is a `:nav`.

```
:import std.nav

:nav
```

A page says where it goes with exported variables:

| Variable | |
|:---------|:-|
| `nav.category` | Its group. Pages without one come first. |
| `nav.order` | A number that orders the pages of a group, which are then ordered by title. Groups come in the order of their first page, then by name. |
| `nav.title` | What the menu shows, instead of the page's title. |

```
:export nav.category = Guides
:export nav.order = 2
```

The menu is a `<nav class="nav">` of nested lists; the current page's item has the class `current`, and a group's the class `category`.
